<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">31082026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Eight missiles fell over Jordan early Monday, shot down by Jordanian air defences as the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps claimed it had struck two American bases on Jordanian soil.</s> <s>Amman sits some fifteen hundred kilometres from Larak Island, where American forces hit Iranian launchers on Sunday — and that distance is the whole point, because a state that hosts foreign bases inherits the retaliation aimed at them without ever casting a vote.</s> <s>Jordan's own account and Tehran's describe the same night in incompatible terms, and neither has been independently verified.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>American forces struck Larak Island on Sunday, destroying what officials describe as two Iranian launchers being prepared for sea-mine rockets near the narrowest point of the Strait of Hormuz.</s> <s>That strait carries roughly a fifth of the world's seaborne oil through a channel barely thirty-three kilometres wide at its throat, and mining it has been Iran's declared deterrent since the tanker war of the nineteen-eighties.</s> <s>Tehran's account of what was on that island differs from Washington's, and the strait remains the pressure point neither side can afford to lose.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and Turkey convened the first meeting of their Mecca defence pact in Istanbul, and Pakistan sent its deputy prime minister, its defence minister and its army chief together.</s> <s>That full civil-military delegation is itself the message: this is the first standing security architecture in the Muslim world with a permanent secretariat rather than a rotating summit, binding three states of some three hundred and fifty million people, one of them nuclear-armed.</s> <s>It's being built precisely as Gulf capitals discover what hosting foreign bases now costs them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two civilians, including a sixteen-year-old boy, were killed in a strike on Belgorod on Sunday, with nine more minors injured, according to the region's acting governor.</s> <s>Belgorod, a city of three hundred and forty thousand, sits inside the band where both militaries treat targets as legitimate and civilians absorb the miss distance — eighteen months of reciprocal border fire have turned it into a casualty ledger neither government publishes.</s> <s>The only source in our feed is Russian state media, so treat every figure as an official claim rather than an established fact.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nicolás Maduro posted photographs of himself from a Brooklyn jail cell to his own social channels, seven months after an American raid on Caracas seized him.</s> <s>Venezuela's former president awaits trial next June, and his successor Delcy Rodríguez now governs a country whose head of state was removed by another country's courts — a template with no modern precedent.</s> <s>What that template means for every other government Washington has indicted is the question nobody in the region is asking out loud.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Donald Trump has asked American regulators to punish the NBC anchor Kristen Welker over an editorial dispute.</s> <s>The Federal Communications Commission licenses individual stations, not networks, so the threat lands not on the anchor but on the local broadcasters who carry her — an old lever, rarely pulled this openly since the Nixon years.</s> <s>Disney's already suing over a related matter, and the courts haven't yet said where editorial judgment ends and licensable conduct begins.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Nigeria's Plateau State, Pastor Hills Emmanuel was found dead near the roadside where gunmen seized him and eight other minivan passengers.</s> <s>The Jos to Bokkos road has become a ransom economy rather than a sectarian frontier, and conflating the two has repeatedly sent the wrong response to the wrong problem.</s> <s>A second pastor is still held, and his family's waiting for a call.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two allied armed groups have overrun the Mirebalais region of Haiti, a district that until recently had escaped the capital's collapse.</s> <s>Police and the army now share territorial control with civilian self-defence militias, which is how displacement stops being an emergency and becomes a permanent arrangement.</s> <s>Residents there now depend for protection on neighbours with rifles, not on any state.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>American Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent says another bank will be designated this week over Iran, and he declines to name it.</s> <s>His last promised major financial institution turned out to be Banque Misr, Egypt's second-largest retail bank — a lender for ordinary depositors, not a conduit for Tehran.</s> <s>Correspondent-banking designations work by frightening third-country banks into over-compliance, so the measurable harm reaches shopkeepers with dollar accounts long before it reaches anyone in Iran.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington's asking the G20 to press Beijing collectively to shrink its export surplus and consume more at home.</s> <s>China's one-point-two trillion dollar surplus is the mirror image of a domestic demand shortfall Beijing's declined to fix for a decade, and the countries being recruited — India, Brazil, Turkey, Nigeria — depend on exactly the cheap Chinese goods that hold their own consumer prices down.</s> <s>The G20 has no instrument to compel anyone, which suggests the real aim is the tariff coordination that would follow.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The yen broke past one hundred and sixty to the dollar on Monday.</s> <s>Japanese households now pay for imported energy in a strengthening dollar during a Hormuz disruption while their own currency weakens — two pressures moving against them at once, driven by the Bank of Japan's rate gap with the Federal Reserve.</s> <s>The Ministry of Finance hasn't intervened, and history says selling reserves buys weeks, not a reversal.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Punjab's Healthcare Commission sealed one thousand four hundred and fifteen unlicensed clinics in six weeks, after six thousand three hundred and eighty raids.</s> <s>Roughly one in four premises inspected was practising medicine without qualification, in a province of one hundred and twenty-seven million where these clinics are what people priced out of licensed care actually use.</s> <s>A regulator can close a clinic, but it can't create the doctor who'd replace it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uzbekistan will supply India with uranium outside Moscow's orbit, in a deal signed as leaders gathered in Bishkek for the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation summit.</s> <s>Uzbekistan ranks among the world's largest producers, and the pact pulls fuel away from Russian and Chinese supply chains for Indian reactors — while Narendra Modi met Vladimir Putin at a summit Washington doesn't attend, buying discounted Russian crude under American tariff pressure.</s> <s>The Shanghai grouping can't act as a bloc, but it's where the sanctions-exposed go to arrange the workarounds.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A refinery at Kulevi in Georgia took its first cargo of Libyan oil on Friday, dropping Russian crude.</s> <s>European sanctions would bite in January of twenty twenty-seven if it kept processing Russian barrels, and Georgia's government has spent two years positioning itself as Moscow-friendly.</s> <s>Commercial arithmetic, it turns out, moved faster than politics.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A phase two trial in Shanghai reported an eighty-one and a half percent response rate for an antibody-drug conjugate in patients with so-called HER2-low breast cancer.</s> <s>Those patients were until recently told they were HER2-negative and ineligible for targeted therapy — the category didn't exist as treatable until these drugs made it one, and much of that development has shifted to Chinese pharmaceutical firms.</s> <s>A phase two is a signal, not an approval, and larger randomised trials are still needed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Square Kilometre Array, the largest radio telescope ever built, is pairing its own data with the sky knowledge of the Karoo and Wajarri communities whose land it occupies.</s> <s>Big science normally treats a site as empty, and the world's largest instruments are increasingly built in the Global South for the radio quiet — making the status of host communities a design decision rather than an afterthought.</s> <s>Whether collaboration outlasts construction is the part nobody can promise yet.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chemists have demonstrated a cut-to-fuse method that rebuilds a molecule's carbon backbone rather than the groups hanging off it.</s> <s>Synthesis has always worked outward from a fixed skeleton, so a failed drug candidate meant starting over from raw materials — editing the frame itself collapses months of work into a step.</s> <s>How broadly it generalises beyond the published examples isn't yet known.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Maintainers of kernel dot org report fourteen processor cores rendering commit pages continuously for artificial intelligence crawlers that ignore robots dot txt and rotate addresses to evade blocks.</s> <s>They're reharvesting one and a half million commits across nine hundred and twenty-two duplicate forks — from the donation-funded infrastructure hosting the source code nearly every server, phone and router on earth runs on.</s> <s>The commons assumed human-scale reading, and the people paying the bandwidth bill have no way to invoice anyone.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A face licensed once for a single AI-generated advertisement in China can be reused indefinitely.</s> <s>Consent law for likeness was built around a per-use economy — one shoot, one campaign, one fee — and generative models break that assumption completely, so models and ordinary people now appear in campaigns they agreed to exactly once.</s> <s>China's labelling rules address disclosure but say nothing about how long a signature lasts, and neither does anyone else's.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Unreleased builds from dozens of game publishers have leaked from Valve's Steam platform through a public interface, not a break-in.</s> <s>The depot system kept delisted builds addressable online for years after they left sale — a design choice made when nobody was systematically enumerating them.</s> <s>Valve hasn't commented, and the archive keeps spreading.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Elazığ, Turkey, built a rooftop system that captures the waste heat that normally degrades solar cell efficiency and sells it back as a second energy product, generating forty-three percent more power than the building needed.</s> <s>Financial payback runs seven to thirteen years, which is the number that decides whether a design spreads or stays in a journal.</s> <s>Whether those figures hold outside Elazığ's particular sun and climate is the open question, in sha'Allah answered by the next installations.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>